findings.body:
If `body` contains attacker-controlled HTML (e.g. `<script>`, `<img onerror>`, or event handlers), it executes directly in every viewer's browser.

```suggestion
// render rich formatting via a safe markdown renderer or sanitizer
// (example: use a library that returns a sanitized string)
return <div className="comment" dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: sanitize(body) }} />;
```
